  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Proposed demolition of the existing side garage and rear extension and replaced with a front,side and rear single storey extension.  Internal reconfiguration.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 5pt; margin-right: 0cm; margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;The\r\nproposed ground floor rear extension, by virtue of its significant mass, depth\r\nand height would result in&amp;nbsp;&lt;span pt=&quot;&quot; sans=&quot;&quot;&gt;an unreasonable degree of visual&amp;nbsp;impacts and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;create an undue sense of enclosure to the rear of the\r\nNo. 9 Cuckoo Hill Drive. The associated window to the flank elevation of the\r\nproposed ground floor rear extension would also result in increased overlooking\r\nand a loss of privacy to No. 9 Cuckoo Hill Drive. The proposal is therefore\r\ncontrary to the National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3.D(7) of the London Plan (2021), policy\r\nDM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and the\r\nadopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;PT Sans&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal, by reason of the site being\r\nlocated within an area of land liable to flooding and the lack of a\r\ncomprehensive Flood Risk Assessment, due to a lack of compensatory flood storage details, has failed to demonstrate that the proposed\r\ndevelopment would not exacerbate the risk of flooding within the site or\r\nincrease the risk and consequences of flooding elsewhere, contrary to the\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies SI12 and SI13 of The London\r\nPlan (2021), Core Policy CS1.U of Harrow Core Strategy (2012) and Policies DM 9\r\nand DM 10 of the Harrow Development Management Polices Local Plan (2013).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
